          %h2#introduction Introduction
          %p
            This article is about structure on a closed interval of real numbers, generally taken to be
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = [0, 1]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra+of+an+endofunctor"} coalgebraic
            perspective. This topic was introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"} Peter Freyd
            in a
            %a{:href => "#Freydcomment"} posting
            about the
            %a{:href => "#PavlovicPratt"} paper
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dusko+Pavlovic"} Dusko Pavlovic
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vaughan+Pratt"} Vaughan Pratt
          %h2#coalgebraic_description_of_
            Coalgebraic description of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            For the moment we work
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classically
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
            %em bipointed set
            is a set equipped with two elements, that is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 0
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  1 &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 \\
                  \&amp; ^\mathllap{x_0} \searrow &amp; &amp; \swarrow^\mathrlap{x_1} &amp; \\
                  \&amp; &amp; X &amp; &amp;
                  }
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1
            might coincide. There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal product
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cospan
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cospan(1, 1)
            given by cospan composition (formed by taking
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∨
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x_0,x_1) \vee (Y,y_0,y_1)
            is
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊎
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((X \uplus Y)/(x_1 \sim y_0), x_0, y_1)
            = succeed "-element" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cos
          %p
            Inside
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cos
            is the full subcategory of
            %em two-pointed
            sets, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1
            are distinct. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Twop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop
            be the category of two-pointed sets. The monoidal product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∨
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee
            restricts to a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Twop
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Twop
                  %mo →
                  %mi Twop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee \colon Twop \times Twop \to Twop
          %p and one can define the square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sq
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Twop
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                  %mi Twop
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Twop
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ∨
                  %mi Twop
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq = (Twop \stackrel{\Delta}{\to} Twop \times Twop \stackrel{\vee}{\to} Twop)
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sq
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq
              \-coalgebra
            is a two-pointed set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            together with a map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi: X \to X \vee X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = [0, 1]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \vee I
            is identified with the interval
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, 2]
            and the coalgebra structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \to I \vee I
            is identified with multiplication by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, 1] \to [0, 2]
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_freyd Theorem (Freyd)
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (I, \alpha)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+coalgebra+for+an+endofunctor"} terminal
              in the category of
              = succeed "-coalgebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sq
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq
          %h2#corecursively_defined_operations_on_
            Corecursively defined operations on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            We now define a number of operations on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq x \leq 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi min
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \uparrow} \coloneqq \min(2 x, 1)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi max
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \downarrow} \coloneqq \max(2 x - 1, 0)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            which can also be defined as maps in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cos
            using the coalgebra structure
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi α
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ∨
                      %mo !
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∨
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \stackrel{{(-) \uparrow}}{\to} I = (I \stackrel{\alpha}{\to} I \vee I \stackrel{I \vee !}{\to} I \vee 1 \cong I)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi α
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo !
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi I
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi I
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \stackrel{{(-) \downarrow}}{\to} I  = (I \stackrel{\alpha}{\to} I \vee I \stackrel{! \vee I}{\to} 1 \vee I \cong I)
          %p
            We similarly define unary operations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {(-)\uparrow}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {(-) \downarrow}
            for any
            = succeed "-coalgebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sq
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \xi)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \downarrow} = x_0
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \uparrow} = x_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_0 \colon X \to X \vee X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1 \colon X \to X \vee X
            are the evident pushout inclusions, we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi(x) = i_0({x \uparrow})
            if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \downarrow} = x_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi(x) = i_1({x \downarrow})
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \uparrow} = x_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0, x_1
            and two unary operations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \uparrow
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \downarrow
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mi or
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash {x \uparrow} = x_1 or {x \downarrow} = x_0
          %h3#ordertheoretic_operations Order-theoretic operations
          %p
            Next, we define meet and join operations on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \downarrow} = 0
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mo ≤
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \uparrow} \leq {y \uparrow}
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {y \uparrow} = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mo ≤
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \downarrow} \leq {y \downarrow}
          %p
            If one prefers to work with operations, one could define the meet operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge \colon I \times I \to I
            by putting a suitable coalgebra structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \times I
            and using terminality of the coalgebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            to define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge
            as a coalgebra map. A coalgebra structure
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \colon I \times I \to (I \times I) \vee (I \times I)
          %p which works is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mo ,
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi(x, y) = i_0({x \uparrow}, {y \uparrow})
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \downarrow} = 0
                or
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {y \downarrow} = 0
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo ,
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi(x, y) = i_1({x \downarrow}, {y \downarrow})
                if
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x \uparrow} = 1 = {y \uparrow}
          %h3#midpoint_operations Midpoint operations
          %p The general midpoint operation is not as easy to construct as one might think, but to start with we do have operations which take the midpoint between a given point and an endpoint. Namely, the left midpoint operation is the unary operation defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi l
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 0
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi α
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l = (I \stackrel{i_0}{\to} I \vee I \stackrel{\alpha^{-1}}{\to} I)
          %p and the right midpoint operation is defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi α
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = (I \stackrel{i_1}{\to} I \vee I \stackrel{\alpha^{-1}}{\to} I).
          %h2#constructive_aspects Constructive aspects
          %p
            There are two versions of this construction, classically equivalent, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MacNeille+real+numbers"} MacNeille real numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+Dedekind+real+numbers"} located Dedekind real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cos
            (which is straightforward) but define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Twop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop
            differently, and the monoidal product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∨
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee
            is subtler.
          %p
            For the MacNeille real numbers, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Twop
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop_M
            in the most obvious way,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\; x_0 = x_1 .
          %p
            For the Dedekind real numbers, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Two
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Two_D
            by requiring
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ¬
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∨
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ¬
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x,\; \neg\; x = x_0 \;\vee\; \neg\; x = x_1 .
          %p
            (The two statements are equivalent assuming the classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+law"} de Morgan law
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg(p \wedge q) \Rightarrow \neg{p} \vee \neg{q}
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \vee Y
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y) \in X \vee Y
            iff
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ¬
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∧
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ¬
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\neg\; x = x_1 \;\Rightarrow\; y = y_0) \;\wedge\; (\neg\; y = y_0 \;\Rightarrow\; x = x_1) .
          %p
            (A pushout can be constructed using
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∨
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x_1 \;\vee\; y = y_0
            instead; this is stronger in intuitionistic logic but equivalent assuming
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+proposition"} stable
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            As in the classical case, this makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Twop
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop_M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Twop
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop_D
            into “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"}> semigroup
            al” categories (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            but without the monoidal unit), since the unit object (which exists in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cos
            as the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Twop
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop_M
            or in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Twop
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop_D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sq
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq_M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sq
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq_D
            and consider their coalgebras. As stated above,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]_M
            is the final coalgebra of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sq
                      %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq_M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1] = [0,1]_D
            is the final coalgebra of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sq
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq_D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
            Another approach to the Dedekind real interval looks simpler from the perspective of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+analysis"} constructive analysis
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Set
                      %mo #
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_\#
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point%E2%80%93point+apartness+spaces"} point–point apartness spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+extensional+functions"} strongly extensional functions
            between them. (A point–point apartness space is a set equipped with an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#
            satisfying properties
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"} dual
            to those of an equivalence relation; it is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            iff the apartness relation is
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+relation"} tight
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo #
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} #
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cos
                      %mo #
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cos_\#
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \vee Y
            be the subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
            satisfying
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo #
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∧
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo #
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \# x_1 \;\Rightarrow\; y = y_0) \;\wedge\; (y \# y_0 \;\Rightarrow\; x = x_1) .
          %p
            Define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Twop
                    %mo #
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop_\#
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo #
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∨
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo #
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \# x_0 \;\vee\; x \# x_1 .
          %p
            Now defining
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sq
                    %mo #
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sq_\#
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Twop
                      %mo #
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Twop_\#
          %h2#computational_aspects Computational aspects
          %p … explain how the classical version corresponds to computation with (unsigned) binary digits … the constructive (Dedekind) version corresponds to computation with signed binary digits …
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#PavlovicPratt
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dusko+Pavlovic"}> Dusko Pavlovic
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vaughan+Pratt"} Vaughan Pratt
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On coalgebra of real numbers
                %strong 19
                (1999) 103-117, doi:
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S1571-0661%2805%2980272-5"}> 10.1016/S1571-0661(05)80272-5
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.47.5204"} CiteSeerx
            %li#Freydcomment
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
                ,
                %em Real coalgebra
                Mailing to the categories list, Dec. 22, 1f999. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.mta.ca/~cat-dist/catlist/1999/realcoalg"}> link
                )
          %p The constructive version is also due to Freyd:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Reality Check
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://facultypages.ecc.edu/alsani/ct99-00%288-12%29/msg00200.html"} web
          %p Freyd published 8 years later:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Real Analysis
              %strong 20
              no.10 (2008) pp. 215–306. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/20/10/20-10abs.html"}> web
              )
          %p
            There is also a complete development in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sketches of an Elephant
